WEBVTT

00:04.000 --> 00:06.533
Specialized vehicles such as aerial work platforms and ladder trucks

00:06.533 --> 00:09.466
are typically used for low-speed driving and short-distance trips

00:09.466 --> 00:12.333
they are primarily operated at low speeds and over short distances,

00:12.333 --> 00:15.966
and all work is performed while the vehicle is stationary,

00:15.966 --> 00:20.966
work time accounts for approximately 55% or more of the total operating time.

00:20.966 --> 00:23.599
Fuel consumption resulting from the engine running while stationary

00:23.599 --> 00:26.233
accounts for approximately 38% of total fuel consumption,

00:26.233 --> 00:28.733
resulting in economic losses as well as emissions

00:28.733 --> 00:31.599
exhaust fumes and noise emitted around the worksite.

00:31.599 --> 00:34.733
To address these issues, ROC Auto Systems has

00:34.733 --> 00:39.066
reusing high-voltage batteries from electric vehicles and drive systems from hybrid vehicles

00:39.066 --> 00:43.633
to develop the e-PTO system, which electrifies aerial work platforms.

00:45.166 --> 00:48.300
To this end, we conducted performance verification on the reused components.

00:48.300 --> 00:51.433
The results of the performance verification for the hybrid vehicle drive system

00:51.433 --> 00:55.833
Despite the power drive converter having reached the end of its service life,

00:55.833 --> 00:58.400
it was found that there was no performance degradation.

00:58.400 --> 01:01.933
Next are the performance verification results for the electric vehicle’s high-voltage battery,

01:01.933 --> 01:07.266
which showed that performance was maintained at approximately 80% or higher compared to a new battery.

01:09.066 --> 01:12.766
To electrify aerial work platforms, we have independently developed an e-PTO Control Unit and

01:12.766 --> 01:15.733
a Motor Control Unit.

01:15.733 --> 01:20.366
In addition, along with the drive motor and inverter—which are reused components from hybrid vehicles—

01:20.366 --> 01:24.466
the e-PTO Control Unit and the e-PTO hydraulic pump,

01:24.466 --> 01:29.800
into a single package to improve installability and serviceability.

01:29.800 --> 01:33.766
In addition, for the high-voltage battery—a reusable component from electric vehicles—

01:33.766 --> 01:37.599
we developed a casing to improve cooling performance and protect the battery, and

01:37.599 --> 01:40.333
and is equipped with a charging system that includes an On-Board Charger

01:40.333 --> 01:43.433
and a charging port to support slow charging.

01:43.433 --> 01:46.500
ROC Auto System’s electrified vehicles

01:46.500 --> 01:50.933
can be charged via a standard slow-charging plug, just like conventional electric vehicles, and

01:50.933 --> 01:54.199
the electrification of ROC Auto System’s e-PTO system

01:54.199 --> 01:57.066
can save approximately 1,300 liters of fuel per year,

01:57.066 --> 01:02:01.066
resulting in greenhouse gas emissions reductions of approximately 3.5 tons.
